{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":447158,"duration_api_ms":493569,"num_turns":39,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"99599e20-e696-401c-9a65-e9b0b2c0ef7c","total_cost_usd":2.5637252499999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":3111,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101165,"cache_read_input_tokens":1966456,"output_tokens":15021,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":101165,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3125,"outputTokens":19855,"cacheReadInputTokens":2203263,"cacheCreationInputTokens":152015,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.5637252499999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"The fallback_all_co2 path (chemistry.rs:85-92) reports all DIC as CO2 with zero HCO3-/CO3--, yet the pH is computed from acid_only_fallback_ph which implies nonzero HCO3-. At the clamped pH of 5.5, HCO3- should be ~12% of CO2 (10^(5.5-6.35) ≈ 0.14). The species output is thermodynamically inconsistent with the reported pH. This causes bicarbonate_mg_total to be artificially zeroed in low-alkalinity water, slightly distorting TDS/conductivity for those regimes. Fix: call carbonate_species_for_ph at the solved (clamped) pH instead of hardcoding all DIC as CO2, or document why the inconsistency is acceptable.","rationale":"Acceptance criteria require the solver to be numerically stable and produce inspectable outputs. An inconsistency between reported pH and species fractions could confuse users inspecting snapshot data in low-alk scenarios (e.g., the ro_like preset transitioning to soft_acidic source water). The magnitude is small but the fix is trivial."},{"body":"The design contract (docs/carbonate_state_contract.md line 112) specifies that fallback paths should 'emit a structured diagnostic' when triggered. The implementation in fallback_all_co2, fallback_high_buffer, and fallback_outside_quadratic_envelope (chemistry.rs:85-118) silently returns results without any logging or tracing. Add at minimum a tracing::debug! or equivalent so operators can detect when the solver hits edge cases during gameplay.","rationale":"The contract explicitly requires structured diagnostics in fallback paths to make 'the bad input regime inspectable.' Without any logging, silent fallback activation during gameplay could mask configuration bugs in source water profiles or process parameters that push the system into degenerate regimes."},{"body":"No integration test verifies that the shipped source water profiles (hard_shrimp, moderate, soft_acidic, ro_like) produce meaningfully differentiated initial pH values from the new solver. Add a test that constructs WaterState from each profile and asserts ordering (e.g., hard_shrimp pH > moderate pH > soft_acidic pH) and minimum spread (e.g., at least 0.3 pH units between hardest and softest).","rationale":"Acceptance criteria explicitly state 'shipped source waters now produce meaningfully differentiated pH values.' The solver unit tests verify correctness of the solver itself, but no test proves the preset profiles actually produce different pH outcomes. A regression in profile DIC/Alk values could eliminate pH differentiation without breaking any existing test."},{"body":"The v2→v3 migration (save.rs:283-314) rescales bicarbonate_mg_total along with all dissolved fields, but normalize_loaded_carbonate_state (save.rs:339-348) unconditionally overwrites it after all migrations complete. The migration rescale of bicarbonate_mg_total is dead work. Consider removing it from the dissolved_fields list with a comment explaining that bicarbonate is now solver-derived, to avoid misleading future migration authors into thinking bicarbonate rescaling is load-bearing.","rationale":"Maintainability concern. A future developer writing a migration that touches bicarbonate_mg_total might copy this pattern without realizing the value is always overwritten post-migration. The comment at nitrogen_cycle.rs:351-352 acknowledges bicarbonate is solver-derived, but the migration code doesn't reflect this understanding."}],"summary":"Reviewed the carbonate equilibrium solver, save/migration system, snapshot integration, and hourly engine pipeline. The core solver is mathematically correct: the pKa1 formula matches Harned & Davis (1943), the quadratic derivation is algebraically sound, and species conservation holds across the normal operating range. The pH clamp, root-selection logic, and fallback paths are numerically stable. All 203 tests pass. DIC/Alk are correctly authoritative; pH and bicarbonate are properly derived. The engine step ordering ensures no stale-pH reads between alkalinity mutations and carbonate resolves. Every system that mutates DIC or alkalinity (nitrogen cycle, plant growth, algae growth, shrimp, water changes) correctly resolves carbonate state afterward. The migration chain is well-structured with compile-time length enforcement. Found four issues: (1) species-pH inconsistency in the zero-alkalinity fallback path, (2) missing structured diagnostics in fallback paths as required by the design contract, (3) no integration test proving source water pH differentiation, and (4) dead bicarbonate rescaling in the v2→v3 migration."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ce6e6303-2a5c-427b-8d44-ee922c2d4292"}
